 "overview": "This file consists of Report No. 43, dated March 16, 1933, filed under State Department decimal file 894.321 (Japanese naval personnel and commissioned officers). The report compiles a comprehensive roster of Imperial Japanese Navy commissioned officers assigned to shore duty and diplomatic posts abroad, extracted from the official Japanese Naval Register of February 1, 1933. It categorizes personnel by host country—including the United States, England, France, Germany, Italy, Russia, China, Manchukuo, Mexico, and a combined mission for Argentina, Brazil, and Chile—and details their ranks, assignments (such as Naval Attaché and Assistant Naval Attaché), and specialized naval branches including Line, Engineering, Medical, Paymaster, Construction, and Ordnance.",
