   "summary": "Report No. 43, dated March 16, 1933, presents an intelligence compilation of Imperial Japanese Navy officers on shore duty overseas derived from the Japanese Naval Register of February 1, 1933. The roster documents postings across the United States, England, France, Germany, Italy, Russia, China, Manchukuo, Mexico, and South America (Argentina, Brazil, and Chile). In addition to accredited naval attachés and assistant attachés, the report enumerates naval specialists by branch, including Line, Engineer, Medical, Paymaster, Construction, Construction-Engineer, and Ordnance officers. It reflects Japan's extensive foreign technical surveillance apparatus in Western nations as well as heightened military postings in China and Manchukuo.",
